from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=R/'docs';p=D/'dev-log/index.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
entry='''<section class="entry" id="ledge-hero-actions" aria-labelledby="ledge-hero-actions-title"><p class="date">3 November 2026 · Ledge contacts and high-drop landing</p><h2 id="ledge-hero-actions-title">Grab the ledge, then keep the landing readable</h2>
<p>The creator asked for a jump beside a high wall to catch its ledge and pull up, plus a superhero landing with one knee down, the opposite fist grounded and the other elbow raised. The earlier short mantle had no sustained hang. The new <a href="../kimodo-game/?controls=hybrid&amp;course=ledge">high-ledge trial</a> uses a purple 2.65 m platform; <a href="../kimodo-game/?controls=hybrid&amp;course=hero-landing">the drop trial</a> starts above a clear landing pad. The footer Action trials selector replays either setup on the chosen body.</p>
<p>The ledge sequence has load, leap, catch, hang, pull-up, top-out and settle phases over 2.45 seconds. Hand targets stay fixed at the lip during the catch/hold, then release during the pull-up. Calibration measures the original rigs' shoulder heights, arm reach and limb lengths after normalization to 1.9 m. The landing point must have standing clearance; hand-width checks reject corners without room for both grips. Existing low barriers retain the shorter vault/mantle behavior. Tagged walls at least 1.9 m high use the ledge sequence, up to a 2.85 m limit; this is not unlimited wall climbing. C releases the ledge, and an attack also releases it into gravity.</p>
<p>A real downward impact after at least a 1.6 m drop and 4.5 m/s downward speed selects the superhero landing. Small standing and high jumps retain their normal landing behavior. The authored pose plants the right knee and left fist, keeps the left foot supported and bends the right elbow upward. A short compression leads into the pose hold and a smooth standing recovery over 1.65 seconds. Fresh movement, C, attacks or Space can replace the recovery. Facing is held during the contact pose so orbiting the camera does not drag the planted fist across the floor.</p>
<p>These are authored pose/contact layers and controller trajectories over the existing generated mantle and hard-landing sources. No fresh Kimodo inference was run for this round, and the 94-type source catalog, two seeds, original meshes and default packs remain unchanged. Two-bone solving preserves segment lengths; knee-shell offsets are calibrated for these two robot meshes. The new runtime layers are included by Record / Save take. Original source and in-place pack exports retain their earlier semantics and exclude runtime contact/controller layers. The recorded samples below contain a continuous climb, walk off the platform, fall, hero landing and recovery.</p>
<p>Testing uncovered two useful controller defects. Floor support used a narrower footprint than horizontal collision, so an actor could begin falling while still overlapping an edge and become stuck against the wall. Both now use the same capsule-footprint radius. At action completion the old clip could also be sampled at an unrelated local clock for one frame while the next asynchronous clip loaded. Holding the last evaluated source time until replacement removes that discontinuity. Traversal source pelvis lift fades out at top-out instead of reappearing after the controller flight finishes. Comparison now follows actor facing, rather than sliding the second model through the wall when the camera orbits; it remains a pose mirror without independent collision.</p>
<p>On both bodies, checks cover reachable ledges, locked hand joint targets, top-out clearance and continuity, real platform drops, knee/fist surface clearance, raised elbow, ordinary-hop exclusion, recovery interruption, ledge release and recording/export. Two recorded GLBs pass structural validation with zero errors and warnings. This establishes the tested controller/contact recipe, not a physically simulated climb or acceptance of every silhouette. Hands, armor, self-collision and transitions still need visual review at different approach angles and speeds.</p>
<p class="evidence">Evidence: <a href="https://github.com/jelaludo/c08-motion-lab/blob/main/research/kimodo/contact-actions-validation.json">contact/action checks</a> · <a href="https://github.com/jelaludo/c08-motion-lab/blob/main/research/kimodo/contact-actions.json">recipe, source hashes and recorded-take mapping</a> · <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jelaludo/c08-motion-lab/main/research/kimodo/contact-takes/c08-ledge-hero-recording.glb">recorded C08 GLB</a> · <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jelaludo/c08-motion-lab/main/research/kimodo/contact-takes/brek43-ledge-hero-recording.glb">recorded B-REK43 GLB</a>. Props and environment meshes are excluded from character recordings.</p><a class="back-top" href="#top">Back to entry index</a></section>'''
